{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HGH9joVf7r2rtT4MbzzWKR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# tasks-api\n2\t\n3\tBackend of a small social to-do app: your tasks are private by default, or\n4\tpublic so friends can see, comment on, like and nudge them. Python standard\n5\tlibrary only, in-memory store (re-seeded on every start).\n6\t\n7\t```\n8\tpython3 api.py                 # http://127.0.0.1:58246\n9\tpython3 -m unittest discover -s tests\n10\t```\n11\t\n12\tEvery request needs `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Development tokens:\n13\t\n14\t| user  | token                    |\n15\t|-------|--------------------------|\n16\t| alice | `tok_alice_4f8c2e71b0`   |\n17\t| bob   | `tok_bob_9a1d7c3e55`     |\n18\t\n19\tSeed data: alice has a private task (#1, \"Draft the investor update\") and a\n20\tpublic one (#2, \"Water the office plants\"); bob has a public task (#3).\n21\t\n22\t## Endpoints\n23\t\n24\t| method | path                     | who                         |\n25\t|--------|--------------------------|-----------------------------|\n26\t| GET    | /tasks                   | own + public tasks          |\n27\t| POST   | /tasks                   | `{\"title\", \"visibility\": \"private\"\\|\"public\"}` |\n28\t| GET    | /tasks/{id}              | owner; anyone if public     |\n29\t| PATCH  | /tasks/{id}              | owner                       |\n30\t| DELETE | /tasks/{id}              | owner                       |\n31\t| POST   | /tasks/{id}/comments     | owner; anyone if public (`{\"text\"}`) |\n32\t| POST   | /tasks/{id}/complete     | owner                       |\n33\t| POST   | /tasks/{id}/nudge        | owner; anyone if public     |\n34\t| POST   | /tasks/{id}/like         | owner; anyone if public     |\n35\t| POST   | /tasks/{id}/view         | owner; anyone if public     |\n36\t\n37\tRule: a private task is visible and touchable only by its owner (403 for\n38\tanyone else, 401 without a token).\n39\t\n40